{
  "source": "course-assets/people-skills/people-skills.mp4",
  "duration": 141.6533125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.98,
      "text": "Your group just finished this semester's history project,"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.98,
      "end": 6.0,
      "text": "but Maya notices a problem with one of the examples"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.0,
      "end": 7.66,
      "text": "and starts suggesting a change."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.4,
      "end": 10.18,
      "text": "Before she can finish, someone interrupts."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.94,
      "end": 12.86,
      "text": "We are done. No more suggestions."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.74,
      "end": 16.9,
      "text": "Maya goes quiet, and the group moves on without addressing her point."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.52,
      "end": 20.26,
      "text": "You notice that Maya's expression and body language changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.8,
      "end": 21.54,
      "text": "She seems hurt."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.12,
      "end": 23.7,
      "text": "What would you say or do next?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.26,
      "end": 25.56,
      "text": "For your next move, say,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.56,
      "end": 27.98,
      "text": "Maya, we didn't hear the rest of your idea."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.36,
      "end": 28.96,
      "text": "Do you wanna finish?"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.88,
      "end": 32.16,
      "text": "This simple question shows her input matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.9,
      "end": 34.6,
      "text": "Maya actually has a valid point."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.06,
      "end": 36.28,
      "text": "The third example they included"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.28,
      "end": 38.04,
      "text": "doesn't match the assignment's instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.58,
      "end": 39.9,
      "text": "By giving her the floor again,"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.26,
      "end": 42.9,
      "text": "the group now possesses the exact information they need"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.9,
      "end": 43.9,
      "text": "to improve their work."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.36,
      "end": 46.0,
      "text": "Her idea deserves to be heard,"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.2,
      "end": 48.04,
      "text": "even if the group decides not to use it."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.64,
      "end": 51.2,
      "text": "What happened with Maya matters beyond this group project."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.82,
      "end": 54.1,
      "text": "People skills matter even more in the AI future."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.1,
      "end": 60.24,
      "text": "First, you'll stand out. As more people use AI, polished work becomes an expectation."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.86,
      "end": 63.16,
      "text": "How you work with people helps you stand out."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.6,
      "end": 65.36,
      "text": "Second, trust still matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.0,
      "end": 70.4,
      "text": "People choose teammates and leaders who listen, keep promises, and treat others well."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.02,
      "end": 72.42,
      "text": "Finally, connection matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.02,
      "end": 77.8,
      "text": "AI can help with the work. People still need to feel heard, understood, and valued."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.34,
      "end": 80.12,
      "text": "You can build these skills starting today."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.54,
      "end": 82.26,
      "text": "Let's walk through four ways to practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.26,
      "end": 84.38,
      "text": "Listen to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.22,
      "end": 87.64,
      "text": "Do not plan your reply while the other person is talking."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.38,
      "end": 91.68,
      "text": "Ask one genuine follow-up question before offering your opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.8,
      "end": 94.38,
      "text": "Notice what isn't being said."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.1,
      "end": 99.62,
      "text": "Pay attention to tone, hesitation, enthusiasm, and changes in behavior."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.26,
      "end": 102.74,
      "text": "If you're unsure what a change means, ask."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.6,
      "end": 104.68,
      "text": "Show people they matter."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.36,
      "end": 106.5,
      "text": "Remember what they tell you."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.84,
      "end": 110.74,
      "text": "Give specific appreciation and give people credit when an idea is theirs."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.74,
      "end": 113.48,
      "text": "Challenge ideas, not people."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.98,
      "end": 116.18,
      "text": "Address difficult things directly and calmly."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.58,
      "end": 118.56,
      "text": "Explain the concern and suggest a way forward."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.28,
      "end": 121.0,
      "text": "This example doesn't match the instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.36,
      "end": 122.14,
      "text": "Could we try another?"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.74,
      "end": 124.64,
      "text": "The group fixes the problem Maya noticed."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.26,
      "end": 126.5,
      "text": "What could you say to give her credit?"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.26,
      "end": 130.52,
      "text": "AI can write it."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.92,
      "end": 132.48,
      "text": "It can't be the person in the room."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.26,
      "end": 134.86,
      "text": "Listen well, speak clearly,"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.22,
      "end": 137.28,
      "text": "and be someone people want to work with."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.74,
      "end": 141.08,
      "text": "Thank you very much."
    }
  ],
